  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The class was designed in response to ships being built by Germany, and it would have rivaled Imperial Japanese and planned American battleships in size, though with less firepower.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383649412:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The Soviets considered as many as fifteen, but eleven were never laid down, and the first four were hampered as Soviet shipbuilding was not ready for ships this large.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383649412:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The Sovetsky Soyuz-class battleships, Project 23, were a class begun by the Soviet Union in the late 1930s, but none were ever brought into service.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383649412:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-02T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On 2 November 2026, 53,573 people read the English article, about 271 times the usual daily figure.",
      "cites": [
